# The official image is built from a repository checkout, not from this folder.
# Keeping the build context out of the image matters: `bin/`, `obj/` and the committed sample
# databases would otherwise be copied in and, worse, invalidate the restore layer on every build.
bin/
obj/
**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
artifacts/

# docs/ is deliberately not excluded. It is 4 MB of Markdown and screenshots, and the dashboard
# project copies observability/grafana-dashboard.json into its build output, so the folder has to be
# in the context or publish fails with MSB3030. Excluding it and punching a hole with a negation rule
# would save nothing worth the indirection.

# A committed store must never become the image's initial database.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

**/*.user
